Falsifies `kernel::arch::x86_64::amd_vi::tests::a_quarantine_blocks_the_alias_too`.

Architecture: x86_64
Environment: NIFE_IOMMU=amd

The defect: `quarantine` blocks the device's own entry and not its alias, which is what it did
before provisional milestone 767 (AMD-Vi hardening before the first AMD boot). A device behind a
PCIe-to-PCI bridge reaches the unit under the alias, so its DMA keeps translating through the
domain the quarantine was meant to take away.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(read_dte(table, alias), blocked_dte(empty), "the quarantined
device's alias still translates")`. Measured on patagonia 2026-10-05 (UTC), QEMU 11.1.1.

